The line serves numerous business commuter pairs within the South Hudur–Haro corridor, including Mazar-Docol, Docol-Badalga, Mazar-Khar, and Iskhal-Docol. The high frequency of express services between these pairs reflects the commercial and economic ties between the cities.

== Stations ==

=== Mazar National Station ===

[[Mazar National Station]] serves as the primary rail terminus for [[Mazar]], one of the major cities of the [[South Hudur]] metropolitan area. The station provides connections to the [[Iskhal-Badalga North Line]] and the [[Mazar-Iskhal Railway]]. The station is the origin for six of the ten service patterns on the South Line.

=== Iskhal Central Station ===

{{main|Iskhal Central Station}}

[[Iskhal Central Station]] is a historic station in the southern part of [[Iskhal]], serving the older districts of the city. The station was extensively remodeled in the late 20th century to accommodate high-speed rail services. The station serves as the convergence point for services originating from Mazar and Iskhal Main, and provides connections to numerous high-speed rail lines.

=== Iskhal Main Station ===

{{main|Iskhal Main Station}}

[[Iskhal Main Station]] is the primary station serving the central business district of [[Iskhal]]. The station serves as the origin for four of the ten service patterns on the South Line (SX2, C, D, G).

=== Docol Central Station ===

[[Docol Central Station]] serves [[Docol]], a major commercial center within the [[South Hudur]] metropolitan area. The station is a key stop for express services, reflecting the strong business travel demand between Docol and other cities.

=== Khar West Station (Caasar) ===

[[Khar West Station]], also known as Caasar, serves the western approach to [[Khar]], a major city in the [[Haro (Metropolitan Administration)|Haro]] metropolitan area. The station is a stop for several express services, providing direct connections to Mazar and Iskhal.

=== Badalga Central Station ===

{{main|Badalga Central Station}}

[[Badalga Central Station]] serves as the northern terminus of the Iskhal-Badalga South Line. The station is integrated with the [[Haro Metro]] system and provides connections to the [[Iskhal-Badalga North Line]], [[Badalga-Laasqoray Line]], [[Badalga-Maianka Line]], and [[Badalga-Khar Line]].

